// @stackup/switch/rkjxv — ALPS RKJXV thumbstick, two potentiometers and a centre push, and the
// hall-effect sticks built as drop-in replacements on its land.

use "@stackup/types"

// ALPS RKJXV122400R: the game-controller analog stick, a lever on two 10 kΩ linear (B taper)
// potentiometers at right angles, 23° each way, with a return spring and a centre push switch.
// RKJXV catalog, Update 2510 (~/dev/datasheets/potentiometer/alps-rkjxv.pdf), Drawing No. 1.
// It replaces the RKJXV1224005, on the same land.
//
// - Potentiometers: 10 kΩ, 5 V DC at most, 12.5 mW. Each is a divider: drive its 1 and 3 from the
//   ADC's reference and ground and read the wiper, 2. Which end is which only sets the sign.
//   VR1 is the column of three down one side, VR2 the row of three across the top.
// - Hall-effect and TMR drop-in sticks (GuliKit and others) are built to this land and pin out the
//   same way, but run a sensor from the ends and drive the wiper from it: they need the ends
//   powered, at the voltage the ADC reads against, and the wiper is an output, not a divider.
// - Switch: 50 mA at 12 V DC, 0.4 mm travel. Four legs, a and c nearer the lever, b and d below
//   them. The catalog does not say which legs are joined inside; a and d, diagonally across, are on
//   opposite sides of the contact whether the legs pair side by side or one above the other.
// - Two locating bosses stand 0.75 mm under the body, in unplated holes the land provides.
// - Through-hole, for hand or selective soldering. No symbol fits, so it borrows the generic
//   ten-way connector with a mounting pin; pads 1-3 are VR1, 4-6 VR2, 7-10 the switch's a, b, c, d.
part rkjxv122400r {
    symbol "Connector_Generic_MountingPin:Conn_01x10_MountingPin"
    reference J
    datasheet "https://tech.alpsalpine.com/e/products/detail/RKJXV122400R/"
    description "Thumbstick, two 10 kΩ potentiometers, 23° each way, centre push switch"
    manufacturer ALPS
    order mpn="RKJXV122400R"

    pin VR1_1 passive
    pin VR1_2 passive
    pin VR1_3 passive
    pin VR2_1 passive
    pin VR2_2 passive
    pin VR2_3 passive
    pin SW_A passive
    pin SW_B passive
    pin SW_C passive
    pin SW_D passive
    pin MP passive

    package tht footprint="stackup:Thumbstick_Alps_RKJXV" {
        pad VR1_1 1
        pad VR1_2 2
        pad VR1_3 3
        pad VR2_1 4
        pad VR2_2 5
        pad VR2_3 6
        pad SW_A 7
        pad SW_B 8
        pad SW_C 9
        pad SW_D 10
        pad MP MP
    }

    port vr1-1 pin=VR1_1
    port vr1-wiper pin=VR1_2
    port vr1-3 pin=VR1_3
    port vr2-1 pin=VR2_1
    port vr2-wiper pin=VR2_2
    port vr2-3 pin=VR2_3
    port sw-a pin=SW_A
    port sw-b pin=SW_B
    port sw-c pin=SW_C
    port sw-d pin=SW_D
    port mp pin=MP
}

// GuliKit hall-effect drop-in stick, sold as a replacement for the RKJXV on its land, with no
// published part number or datasheet. A magnet on the lever and a sensor per axis stand in for the
// potentiometers, so the pins keep the RKJXV's positions but not their meaning: each axis's ends
// power its sensor, 1 to ground and 3 to the supply the ADC reads against, and the wiper, 2, is the
// sensor's output, near half the supply at centre as a potentiometer's would be. Fitted the other
// way round the sensor is reverse-powered, not merely mirrored. Supply range and current are not
// published; the Snips controller runs it from 3.3 V.
//
// The switch legs follow Daniel Benoy's thumbstick-breakout: the two legs in each row are joined
// inside, so the row nearer the lever is one side of the switch and the row below it the other.
// SW_1 and SW_2 are the legs at x = −3.25 mm; SW_1_DUP and SW_2_DUP, their duplicates at +3.25 mm,
// also hold the stick down and can be wired or left `nc`. The ALPS catalog does not say which legs
// are joined on the RKJXV itself (see above), so this pairing is not assumed for that part.
//
// Two lands, the same holes. `gulikit` is the Snips controller's, adapted from thumbstick-breakout:
// larger pads, the pad labels of that design (1–3 and 1′–3′ for the axes, a–d for the switch), and
// no locating-boss holes or keepouts, so a board can route under the stick. `rkjxv` is the ALPS
// land above, with the bosses' holes and the catalog's prohibited wiring areas. Through-hole and
// hand soldered: place it `hand=#true`.
part gulikit-hall-stick {
    symbol "Connector_Generic_MountingPin:Conn_01x10_MountingPin"
    reference J
    value "GuliKit hall stick"
    description "Hall-effect thumbstick, RKJXV drop-in, two ratiometric axes, centre push switch"
    manufacturer GuliKit

    pin VR1_GND power_in
    pin VR1_OUT output
    pin VR1_VCC power_in
    pin VR2_GND power_in
    pin VR2_OUT output
    pin VR2_VCC power_in
    pin SW_1 passive
    pin SW_2 passive
    pin SW_1_DUP passive
    pin SW_2_DUP passive
    pin MP passive

    // The breakout's mounting legs are unnumbered pads, so MP is not bonded in this package.
    package gulikit footprint="stackup:GuliKit_HallStick" {
        pad VR1_GND "1'"
        pad VR1_OUT "2'"
        pad VR1_VCC "3'"
        pad VR2_GND 1
        pad VR2_OUT 2
        pad VR2_VCC 3
        pad SW_1 a
        pad SW_2 c
        pad SW_1_DUP b
        pad SW_2_DUP d
    }
    package rkjxv footprint="stackup:Thumbstick_Alps_RKJXV" {
        pad VR1_GND 1
        pad VR1_OUT 2
        pad VR1_VCC 3
        pad VR2_GND 4
        pad VR2_OUT 5
        pad VR2_VCC 6
        pad SW_1 7
        pad SW_2 8
        pad SW_1_DUP 9
        pad SW_2_DUP 10
        pad MP MP
    }

    port vr1-out type=output pin=VR1_OUT
    port vr2-out type=output pin=VR2_OUT
    port sw-1 pin=SW_1
    port sw-2 pin=SW_2
}
